# Graphical installer (plan §10).
#
# Calamares is the maintained upstream installer. It is NOT written from scratch and
# no custom partitioning program exists in this project (plan §10.1 and Rule 9).
#
# The kpmcore/parted stack below is what Calamares actually uses to identify and
# partition the target disk, so the disk-selection screens show real devices.

calamares
calamares-settings-debian

squashfs-tools
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
ntfs-3g
xfsprogs
btrfs-progs
f2fs-tools
jfsutils
reiserfsprogs
exfatprogs
parted
gdisk
# kpmcore is shipped as a versioned library package in the pinned release. The
# exact major version is asserted by tests/static/test_packages.py.
libkpmcore12
os-prober
grub2-common
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-efi-ia32-bin
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-signed
shim-signed
efibootmgr
efivar

lvm2
cryptsetup
cryptsetup-initramfs
keyutils

# REMOVED: dropbear-initramfs.
# It provides a minimal SSH server inside the initramfs, which exists to allow remote
# unlocking of a root filesystem encrypted with a passphrase. AstraOS does not ship that
# configuration, and disk encryption has never been tested (docs/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md
# §2). Installing an untested network service in the initramfs - the stage that runs
# before any security policy or firewall applies - for a feature nobody has verified is
# not a trade worth making (plan §13.2). Re-add it together with the initramfs network
# configuration, not before.

arch-install-scripts
unattended-upgrades
